# Architecture Plan

## Product Scope

The product is the existing single-page **Simple email sender**. Issues #23
and #24 progressively evolve only its page background: #23 restores a bright
multi-color treatment, then #24 intensifies it into an even brighter rainbow
palette. The email composition and delivery flow remain unchanged.

## Module Structure

- `src/client/App.tsx`: email-composer markup, client-side form state, and send
  feedback; no background-specific logic is required.
- `src/client/styles.css`: document canvas styling and responsive component
  styles. It owns the reusable page-background gradient stack and will contain
  both visual changes.
- `src/client/main.tsx`: client bootstrap and global stylesheet import.
- `src/client/sendEmail.ts` and `src/shared/email.ts`: existing browser/server
  email contract; outside the scope of both background issues.
- `src/server/` and `tests/`: delivery implementation and coverage; unchanged
  unless visual tooling is added in a later task.

## Issue Dependencies

1. Issue #23 establishes the bright multi-color background foundation in
   `src/client/styles.css`, replacing the current blue-only canvas treatment.
2. Issue #24 depends on the palette structure introduced by #23 and adjusts
   the same CSS gradient stops, saturation, and luminance to make the result a
   visibly brighter rainbow without altering layout or functionality.

## Key Design Decisions

- Keep both changes CSS-only on `body`, using layered fixed gradients so the
  background covers the full viewport and remains stable during page overflow.
- Use a small, coherent rainbow palette with adequate brightness while keeping
  the existing opaque white form surface and dark copy for readable content.
- Do not introduce new shared types, dependencies, API changes, or server-side
  behavior for visual-only work.
- Preserve the same selector and gradient-stack structure across the two
  issues so #24 is a focused palette refinement rather than a redesign.
